TITLE:: REKnobMix
summary:: One parameter's mix of a tape value and a knob, with the three states a button chooses
categories:: Libraries>reCording
related:: Guides/reCording, Classes/REShowRoto, Classes/REShowConsole, Classes/REShowChase

DESCRIPTION::
A parameter of HomewareVisuals' effects page has two sources at HadronLake3's show console (link::Classes/REShowConsole::): the take's strong::tape:: value T (what the piece sent as code::/fx/ctl <name> <value>::, replayed by link::Classes/REShowChase::) and a strong::knob:: K of the Roto-Control (link::Classes/REShowRoto::), 0..1. The page keeps the last value it received and ignores code::/fx/set:: while a parameter is mapped, so the mix is made here and sent as one value. With code::op:: code::\add::, code::out = T + lo + k·(hi - lo)::; with code::\scale::, code::out = T × (lo + k·(hi - lo))::. A knob never moved contributes nothing (add: 0; scale: 1). With no tape value yet, code::\add:: counts T as 0 (the knob's offset alone) and code::\scale:: has nothing to send (link::#-value:: is nil).

Three states, chosen by the knob's button (link::#-state::): 1, both live; 2, T sampled and held at the value it had when the state was entered, K live (a hold entered before any tape value holds nothing: T counts 0 for add, nil for scale, until the hold is left); 3, K held, T live. Leaving a hold, the held source converges strong::linearly:: from its held value to its live value over link::#-glide:: seconds (1.0), then follows it; entering a hold mid-glide holds the value the glide stands at. Every method takes code::now:: in seconds, on any one clock: the console gives code::Main.elapsedTime::, a test counts.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
argument:: op
code::\add:: (the default) or code::\scale::.
argument:: lo
argument:: hi
The knob's range: its contribution at k = 0 and at k = 1.
argument:: glide
Seconds a source takes to reach its live value after a hold (1.0; 0 jumps).

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: tape
The tape's live value; code::tape_(v, now):: sets it (nil until one arrived).
METHOD:: knob
The knob's live position, 0..1; code::knob_(k, now):: sets it (nil until it moved).
METHOD:: state
1, 2 or 3; code::state_(n, now):: changes it (anything else is 1). Leaving a hold starts the held source's glide at code::now::.
METHOD:: value
argument:: now
returns:: The output now: nil before anything arrived, and for code::\scale:: without a tape value.
METHOD:: moving
argument:: now
returns:: True while a glide runs, and once more when one has just ended (so that the live value itself goes out): the console sends the value at its rate while this is true.
METHOD:: isHolding
True in states 2 and 3.
METHOD:: contribution
The knob's contribution to the output at a position; nothing for nil (0 or 1 by the op).
argument:: k
METHOD:: op
METHOD:: lo
METHOD:: hi
METHOD:: glide

EXAMPLES::

code::
m = REKnobMix(\add, -0.5, 0.5);
m.tape_(0.3, 0); m.knob_(0.75, 0); m.value(0);   // 0.55: 0.3 + (-0.5 + 0.75)
m.state_(2, 1); m.tape_(0.9, 2); m.value(2);     // 0.55: the tape held at 0.3
m.state_(1, 3); m.value(3.5);                    // 0.85: half way from 0.3 to 0.9, plus 0.25
m.moving(4.5);                                   // false once there
::
